    {
      "id": "note",
      "type": "note",
      "position": [
        -431.0,
        -218.0
      ],
      "description": "Now we want to start mixing signals. The `Distortion` node on the video signal has its `Drive` set to 0, so it isn't doing anything.\n\nLets try plugging the output of `In: Audio` into the `Drive` control tap.",
      "attached": "c_picture"
    },
    {
      "id": "note_2",
      "type": "note",
      "position": [
        -177.0,
        115.0
      ],
      "description": "Plug this",
      "attached": "audio"
    },
    {
      "id": "note_3",
      "type": "note",
      "position": [
        30.0,
        115.0
      ],
      "description": "Into the blue diamond on this",
      "attached": "distortion"
    },
    {
      "id": "note_4",
      "type": "note",
      "position": [
        -429.0,
        -32.0
      ],
      "description": "Once you've done that, the picture should get brighter based on the volume of the audio signal. It should look like horizontal streaks across the image.",
      "attached": "note"
    },
    {
      "id": "note_5",
      "type": "note",
      "position": [
        -427.0,
        108.0
      ],
      "description": "The `Drive` parameter in the `Distortion` node will now have a bunch more settings to control how it is automated. \nFeel free to mess around with it, or check the manual for more info.",
